        <item>
            <title>0.1.5-beta</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:03:20 +0200</pubDate>
            <link>https://typoless.app</link>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>102</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.5-beta</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Corrections</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Short text is no longer passed over. A line like "chekc this todo" reads as another language once the typo takes the letters the recogniser judges by, and Typoless used to leave it alone without saying so.</li>
    <li>A line too short to have a language of its own now follows the message around it, so an email signed with your name is not read as English in the middle of German.</li>
</ul>
<h3>History</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Every correction is kept, including the ones that changed nothing. What Typoless decided not to do is often the thing worth reporting.</li>
    <li>Each entry says which language it read the text as, what it changed, and for anything it did not change, why: a rule you turned off, protected text, a language that is not switched on, or a reply that was a rewrite.</li>
    <li>The list is a table now, with filters for app, language and what happened, and each change is marked where it is rather than the whole stretch between the first and the last.</li>
    <li>A report on the tracker carries all of it, so the first question about a bug report is already answered in it.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
